{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 995016,
  "courseSlug": "vuejs-2-the-complete-guide",
  "courseTitle": "Vue - The Complete Guide (incl. Router & Composition API)",
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "21463384",
      "title": "Working with Refs",
      "lectureOrder": 66,
      "videoOrder": 59,
      "sourceHash": "c0f6ff2a9ae178828401308972b8344f90b5ee2dfc11f5f5bccda921ad8efd58",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.11,
          "end": 3.42,
          "en": "Now here's a lecture",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 3.42,
          "end": 6.68,
          "en": "which I recommend that you do not skip in this module",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 6.68,
          "end": 8.95,
          "en": "because I'm going to show you a different way",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 8.95,
          "end": 12.493,
          "en": "of getting a value out of such a input element.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 13.34,
          "end": 16,
          "en": "Thus far, we're listening to the input event,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 16,
          "end": 19.938,
          "en": "and therefore, with every keystroke, saveInput is fired,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 19.938,
          "end": 22.229,
          "en": "and in the saveInput method,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 22.229,
          "end": 26.26,
          "en": "INDN just saved the current value of the input",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 26.26,
          "end": 29.09,
          "en": "to the current user input data property,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 29.09,
          "end": 32.67,
          "en": "so that we can eventually use that property later",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 32.67,
          "end": 36.75,
          "en": "to assign the entered value to our message.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 36.75,
          "end": 39.07,
          "en": "Alternatively, as you learned before,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 39.07,
          "end": 44.07,
          "en": "we could also use v-model and bind that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 44.15,
          "end": 48.88,
          "en": "to our current user input property like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 48.88,
          "end": 50.65,
          "en": "That is also something you learned about",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 50.65,
          "end": 51.82,
          "en": "in the course before,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 51.82,
          "end": 55.163,
          "en": "then we can omit this input binding here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 56.73,
          "end": 58.62,
          "en": "But whatever approach we use,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 58.62,
          "end": 63.6,
          "en": "we basically log what the user enters with every keystroke.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 63.6,
          "end": 66.16,
          "en": "Sometimes that is what you need, for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 66.16,
          "end": 68.86,
          "en": "because you want to validate the user input",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 68.86,
          "end": 70.55,
          "en": "with every keystroke,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 70.55,
          "end": 73.26,
          "en": "but sometimes that's all just overkill,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 73.26,
          "end": 76.14,
          "en": "and in such cases, Vue has a feature",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 76.14,
          "end": 80.01,
          "en": "that allows you to retrieve values from DOM elements",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 80.01,
          "end": 83.42,
          "en": "when you need them, instead of all the time.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 83.42,
          "end": 85.92,
          "en": "And that feature is called, refs.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 85.92,
          "end": 87.61,
          "en": "Here's how you add it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 87.61,
          "end": 90.02,
          "en": "Instead of adding this event listener,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 90.02,
          "end": 92.12,
          "en": "which you still could add in addition,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 92.12,
          "end": 94.97999999999999,
          "en": "but which we simply won't need any more now,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 94.97999999999999,
          "end": 96.22999999999999,
          "en": "instead of having that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 96.22999999999999,
          "end": 99.68,
          "en": "you add a special attribute to this element,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 99.68,
          "end": 100.993,
          "en": "the ref attribute.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 102.50999999999999,
          "end": 104.55,
          "en": "Just like the key attribute,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 104.55,
          "end": 107.31,
          "en": "which we used with V4 before,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 107.31,
          "end": 111.9,
          "en": "the ref attribute is a non-default HTML attribute.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 111.9,
          "end": 113.75999999999999,
          "en": "So the browser doesn't know it,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 113.75999999999999,
          "end": 116.07,
          "en": "but Vue understands it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 116.07,
          "end": 117.84,
          "en": "You assign a value here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 117.84,
          "end": 120.79,
          "en": "which is any string identifier of your choice,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 120.79,
          "end": 123.063,
          "en": "for example, userText.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 124.34,
          "end": 126.43,
          "en": "But again, this is totally up to you.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 126.43,
          "end": 129.98,
          "en": "And you can also not just add refs to input elements,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 129.98,
          "end": 133.13,
          "en": "you can add them to any HTML element,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 133.13,
          "end": 135.67,
          "en": "to paragraphs, headers, sections,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 135.67,
          "end": 139.06,
          "en": "inputs, text areas, whatever you need.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 139.06,
          "end": 141.02,
          "en": "Now, why am I doing that?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 141.02,
          "end": 146.02,
          "en": "Because Vue detects such refs and stores them internally.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 146.39,
          "end": 148.81,
          "en": "It basically memorizes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 148.81,
          "end": 152.21,
          "en": "that you want access to the input element.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 152.21,
          "end": 155.57999999999998,
          "en": "And in the JavaScript code, you can then get this access.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 155.57999999999998,
          "end": 157.15,
          "en": "Here, in this case,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 157.15,
          "end": 159.32999999999998,
          "en": "inside of the set text method,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 159.32999999999998,
          "end": 162.71,
          "en": "because that's where I need the entered value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 162.71,
          "end": 165.8,
          "en": "Instead of using this approach,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 165.8,
          "end": 170.45,
          "en": "I can now set this message equal to this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 170.45,
          "end": 174.46,
          "en": "and now a special property, which is provided by Vue,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 174.46,
          "end": 177.313,
          "en": "the dollar sign refs property.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 178.18,
          "end": 181.85,
          "en": "Dollar sign refs is a property provided by Vue.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 181.85,
          "end": 186.38,
          "en": "All Vue provided properties start with dollar signs",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 186.38,
          "end": 189.85,
          "en": "to make it clear that this is a built-in property.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 189.85,
          "end": 194.2,
          "en": "This is an object full of key value pairs",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 194.2,
          "end": 197.37,
          "en": "where the keys are the ref identifiers",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 197.37,
          "end": 199.32999999999998,
          "en": "you set up in your template,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 199.32999999999998,
          "end": 200.613,
          "en": "for example, userText.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 201.63,
          "end": 205.663,
          "en": "So here we can access dot userText.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 207.15,
          "end": 211.6,
          "en": "And this now simply points at the DOM object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 211.6,
          "end": 213.82999999999998,
          "en": "for this input element.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 213.82999999999998,
          "end": 215.41,
          "en": "So the JavaScript object,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 215.41,
          "end": 218.43,
          "en": "we can use in vanilla JavaScript as well,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 218.43,
          "end": 221.083,
          "en": "when we got access to a DOM element.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 222.97,
          "end": 226.68,
          "en": "So now here, we can get access to the full input element,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 226.68,
          "end": 228.74,
          "en": "and to show you what this means,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 228.74,
          "end": 232.263,
          "en": "I'll comment this out and log it to the console for now.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 233.3,
          "end": 238.3,
          "en": "If we now open this console and reload,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 238.74,
          "end": 241.25,
          "en": "and then click, set text,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 241.25,
          "end": 244.53,
          "en": "you see the whole input element is locked here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 244.53,
          "end": 248.79,
          "en": "And if we use console.dir, instead of console.log,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 248.79,
          "end": 251.71,
          "en": "and click, set text, again, after reloading,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 251.71,
          "end": 254.52,
          "en": "here is the inspectable object,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 254.52,
          "end": 258.1,
          "en": "and this is really the JavaScript object representation",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 258.1,
          "end": 261.99,
          "en": "of this input element, with all the properties that has.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 261.99,
          "end": 263.9,
          "en": "So this is not Vue specific,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 263.9,
          "end": 266.13,
          "en": "that is the vanilla JavaScript object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 266.13,
          "end": 269.263,
          "en": "we could use and work with in any JavaScript code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 270.66,
          "end": 274.29,
          "en": "And for example, here, we've got this value property.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 274.29,
          "end": 277.06,
          "en": "Essentially, the object we're logging here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 277.06,
          "end": 280.8,
          "en": "is the same one we get access to with event target,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 280.8,
          "end": 283.76,
          "en": "which is why we can access value there as well.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 283.76,
          "end": 286.57,
          "en": "But now we're not doing this with every keystroke,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 286.57,
          "end": 289.86,
          "en": "but instead only when setText is emitted,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 289.86,
          "end": 291.47,
          "en": "which happens when this button,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 291.47,
          "end": 293.83,
          "en": "the set text button, is clicked.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 293.83,
          "end": 296.40999999999997,
          "en": "So now we can access value here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 296.40999999999997,
          "end": 298.343,
          "en": "And with that, if we reload,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 299.81,
          "end": 302.01,
          "en": "and I set detects to, Vue is awesome,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 302.01,
          "end": 305.3,
          "en": "and click, set text, this works as before,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 305.3,
          "end": 308.58,
          "en": "but now we're not logging the input with every keystroke,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 308.58,
          "end": 312.7,
          "en": "but we only extract it with help of that refs feature",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 312.7,
          "end": 314.24,
          "en": "when we need it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 314.24,
          "end": 317.37,
          "en": "And that's why refs is a feature worth knowing,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 317.37,
          "end": 319.743,
          "en": "and why you shouldn't skip this lecture.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
